<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Let the Song be Begun (John Mason Neale)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Personent hodie (Gustav Holst)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1916</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement for unison voices and orchestra</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">On this day earth shall ring (Jane M. Joseph)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">God is love, his the care (Percy Dearmer)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn sung to Holst's arrangement, &quot;Theodoric&quot;</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Long Ago, Prophets Knew</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn to the same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Boys' Carol (Elizabeth Poston)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Tapestry of Carols (Maddy Prior and The Carnival Band)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1987</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording with period instruments</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">12th Century Carol (Wayne Shorter, on Alegria)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">jazz arrangement of the melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Birds (North Sea Radio Orchestra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental version for small ensemble</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chris Squire's Swiss Choir (Chris Squire)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2007</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement with choir</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Intonent hodie voces ecclesie</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">12th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">earlier song for Saint Nicholas, of which the text is probably a parody</span></li></ul></section>
